# Citation metadata for GitHub's "Cite this repository" (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# The software itself is the citation: there is no preferred-citation block, because GitHub shows that
# block instead of the software whenever one exists. The version is the one of the C++ library and the
# Python package (release tag v<version>); the R package carries its own version in
# R/TRexSelector/DESCRIPTION. The method papers are listed as references; the master list with every
# reference of the class documentation is references.bib at the repository root.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the package and the paper of the method you used."
type: software
title: "TRexSelector: T-Rex Selector: High-Dimensional Variable Selection and FDR Control"
abstract: >-
  High-dimensional variable selection with false discovery rate (FDR) control through terminating
  random experiments (the T-Rex selector) in C++, R and Python.
authors:
  - name: "Team T-Rex"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/trexselector/TRexSelector"
url: "https://trexselector.com"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - false discovery rate
  - variable selection
  - high-dimensional statistics
  - T-Rex selector
